From d031b3ec3ea5521a27a45e2292c1a8460645e8c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:15:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): a FluidNC post and a generic 3040 router machine

Add the built-in post "FluidNC" (assets/posts/fluidnc.cps) and the
built-in machine "3040 router (FluidNC)" (assets/machines/fluidnc-3040.mch).
The machine names FluidNC as its post.

The post is grbl.cps with the FluidNC differences: the header states
"FLUIDNC POST - NOT VERIFIED ON A MACHINE" until an owner reports a
clean dry run, and the refusals and comments name FluidNC. The words
are the Grbl 1.1 words: drill cycles as G0/G1/G4 moves, the tool
change as M5, a Z lift, a comment and M0 (no M6: FluidNC's M6 acts
only through a tool changer or macro in its YAML configuration).
Tapping, boring and G41/G42 are refused by name.

The 3040 values are typical for the class and marked for the owner
to confirm. Decisions and their FluidNC wiki pages are in
docs/decisions/3192-fluidnc-post.md.

Pins: script_fluidnc (recorded-stream suite and six dialect pins),
machine_library (the 3040 is offered the FluidNC post), and the
registry-driven conformance goldens.

Fixes #3192

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
